CRASH-10: free the adjacency lists only when both solvers are closed

The hydraulic and water quality solvers share net->Adjlist: openqual()
reuses the lists when the hydraulic solver has built them. Since the fix
for #789, closehyd() and closequal() both free the lists, so closing one
solver leaves the other with a NULL list array. EN_runQ then crashes in
sortnodes(), and EN_runH crashes in marknodes() on its first warning.
Free the lists in each close function only when the other solver is not
open. The last solver to close still frees them, as #789 requires.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-10_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..1bcfc51 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -309,7 +309,9 @@ void  closehyd(Project *pr)
 {
     freesparse(pr);
     freematrix(pr);
-    freeadjlists(&pr->network);
+
+    // Keep the adjacency lists if the quality solver is still using them
+    if (!pr->quality.OpenQflag) freeadjlists(&pr->network);
 }
 
 
diff --git a/src/quality.c b/src/quality.c
index 36c89b9..fe7bca2 100644
--- a/src/quality.c
+++ b/src/quality.c
@@ -412,7 +412,9 @@ int closequal(Project *pr)
         FREE(qual->FlowDir);
         FREE(qual->SortedNodes);
     }
-    freeadjlists(&pr->network);
+
+    // Keep the adjacency lists if the hydraulic solver is still using them
+    if (!pr->hydraul.OpenHflag) freeadjlists(&pr->network);
     return errcode;
 }
 
